From 704bf9b48ebd5f1666b1532495832dd677aba1ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:28:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): tile opens always log an outcome; sidebar focus
 no longer logs a phantom abandoned open [daveey]

The 11-10 @session ref live proof collected two [open-timing] lines for the target, both
startedBy:"click" with no surface: sidebar-row main-pane opens, not the ref chip's tile.
Tracing the entry paths showed:

- markOpenClick (sidebar onResumeSession) is the only writer of startedBy:"click"; a sidebar click
  on a chat already on screen as a tile only fronts the tile, so the record dangled and was flushed
  as outcome:"abandoned" by the next open. Now a click that never entered resumeSession is dropped.
- A tile open that threw (owner/resume failure) or lost a rebind race wrote no line at all, so a
  failed ref click was indistinguishable from no click. It now logs outcome "failed"/"abandoned".
- A cold tile open (REST paint) did not save its REST page, unlike the main pane; it now warms the
  cache under the tile owner key.
- isTileCachePaint/tileCachePaintProof: the acceptance gate for "ref click painted the tile from
  cache" (surface tile + paint cache + outcome rest); main-pane, abandoned, failed and no-paint
  records cannot satisfy it.

Chip -> tile routing and prefetch key are pinned by a new test (passes before and after: not a defect).
